M07_Inn_Evac::Custom formatted the evacuee object id into char param1[10]
with sprintf. Sydney and the three DEAD-6 evacuees are spawned (spawners
103833-103836), so their ids are 10-digit dynamic ids; the text plus the
terminator needs 11 bytes and the stack buffer overflowed on four of the five
evacuations. M07_Inn_APC and M07_APC_Dec have the same pattern (not bound in
retail M07). Enlarge the buffers to 16 bytes and use snprintf so the write is
bounded. The formatted text is unchanged.

--- a/Mission07.cpp
+++ b/Mission07.cpp
@@ -4132,8 +4132,8 @@
 			reinforce++;
 			if(reinforce < 7)
 			{
-				char param1[10];
-				sprintf(param1, "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
+				char param1[16];
+				snprintf(param1, sizeof(param1), "%d", Commands->Get_ID(obj));
 
 				Vector3 pos = Commands->Get_Position(obj);
 				float facing = Commands->Get_Facing(obj);
@@ -5135,8 +5135,8 @@
